  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=5,{x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-4(x-5)(x-(-2))(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =-4(x-5)(x+2)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-5)(x+2)(x+2) & =-4(x-5)({x}^{2}+4x+4) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+4x-5{x}^{2}-20x-20) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20) \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+64x+80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+64x+80.$",
